00:43:12,942 --> 00:43:26,365
If the pair is directly connected to each other, then we can use the natural walking speed model to compute the time taken to travel from one vertex to another.

295
00:43:27,186 --> 00:43:31,373
If they are not directly connected, we introduce some hypothetical edge between them.

296
00:43:33,023 --> 00:43:42,874
which is the shortest path between the pair of vertices, and then compute the travel time from one vertex to another along the shortest path using the natural walking speed.

297
00:43:44,796 --> 00:43:54,707
So, in that way, we compute the travel time, which is the new weight we assign to the graph after converting it to a complete graph by introducing hypothetical edges.

